<div>
  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>The price of bitcoin has seen better days, as the coin’s value hit $59,600 four days ago and then saw the exchange rate tumble to a low of $45,700 per unit on May 12. There have been talks of whales selling coins and data shows that there’s been some large wallet inflows. However, onchain data shows that the whales are either dispersing funds into multiple wallets or bitcoin is being distributed more evenly to smaller fish.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Number of Bitcoin Whales With 1K Bitcoin or More Declines, Sharks, Dolphins, and Small Fish Increase
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    While cryptocurrency markets approach the weekend, traders and speculators are wondering what will happen next with these volatile price changes. During the last 48 hours, bitcoin (BTC) and a myriad of other digital currencies have seen massive fluctuations in fiat value.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    As usual, cryptocurrency participants have been looking at the count of “bitcoin whales,” and have been assuming these large market players have been making massive waves.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-459007 size-full" title="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/sizes.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" width="450" height="301" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/sizes.jpg 450w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/sizes-300x201.jpg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Most people consider a bitcoin (BTC) whale to be a holder that owns 1,000 bitcoin or more. A summary from bitcoinwiki.org states that a whale owns 1,000 to 5,000 BTC. A “humpback whale” or “mega whale” is classified as a BTC owner with 5,000 coins or more.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Now some whales are individuals, and other types of whales are entities like crypto investment funds such as Grayscale Investments’ Bitcoin Trust. During the last few days, a few reports have said that the number of BTC whales in the crypto ocean has been dropping considerably.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-458996 size-full" title="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" width="1280" height="720" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-768x432.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/wm-760x428.jpg 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    People often speculate on BTC whale action, but crypto market spectators only have a few tools they can use to whale watch. Recent reports have leveraged Glassnode’s “Number of Addresses with Balance ≥ 1k” chart in order to visualize bitcoin whales and watch them closely.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Glassnode’s data shows on Wednesday, just over 2,100 whales (addresses holding 1,000 BTC or more) exist, and last year during the same month, 100 more whales existed. This data does not mean whales are selling, as any owner of 1,000 bitcoins in one address can simply split the funds into two addresses or more.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Trickle-Down Distribution or Bitcoin Whale Addresses Morphing Into Multiple Dolphin Addresses
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Some articles claim that BTC is being distributed more to holders with less bitcoin than massive whales, which suggests that whales are selling. Despite these claims, data suggests that whales are distributing bitcoins but could be whale address reorganizations.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    For instance, onchain data from whalemap.io shows signs of whale movements in recent days and large wallet inflows in greater detail. Like Glassnode’s stats, data from whalemap.io implies a decline in whales (balance ≥ 1k) and a downward distribution cycle.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-458997 size-full" title="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" width="2560" height="800" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333.jpg 2560w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-300x94.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-1024x320.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-768x240.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-1536x480.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-2048x640.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-696x218.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-1392x435.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-1068x334.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-1344x420.jpg 1344w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/whales3333-1920x600.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    We also have data stemming from a Bitcoin.com News report published on May 1, 2020. This article also covered the topic of whale counts and noted that whales obtained hundreds of BTC from “small fish.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    It is interesting to note, that three addresses have 100,000 to 1 million BTC held in a single address. This number has not changed in May 2021, and there are still three colossal whale addresses with 100k BTC or more. However, “humpback whale” or “mega whale” addressees have dropped in number and there’s not as many this year.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-458999" title="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Whale Count Shrinks- Speculators Assume Trickle Distribution or Possible Address Reorganizations" width="589" height="331" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-768x432.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/900887777ijhh-760x428.jpg 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 589px) 100vw, 589px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Data from the 2020 article and the current “Bitcoin Rich List” published on bitinfocharts.com, indicates whale addresses with 10,000 to 100,000 bitcoins dipped from 106 addresses to 85. Similar to the concept of “trickle-down economics,” data from bitinfocharts.com alludes to whale addresses dispersing bitcoin to addresses with lower quantities of BTC.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    One could insinuate that whales are distributing coins to “sharks (500 BTC),” “dolphins (100 BTC),” and “fish (50 BTC).” Or the whale addresses could simply be reorganizing into multiple lower quantity addresses that are still maintained by the same owners.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about the bitcoin whale count dropping? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below.</strong></em>
  </p>
</div>
